  "markdown_report": "## Insights\n\n**Starting point.** (1) Feedback favors recent intent and repeated narrow preferences. This motivates separating recent evidence from accumulated preference. (2) Broad associations sometimes outrank supported practical matches. Interaction histories cannot establish equipment ownership or compatibility, so these remain hypotheses. (3) Existing probes measure embedding similarity and sampled margins. Neither establishes useful temporal reasoning or predicts validation gains.\n\n**Related work.** (1) Petrov et al. report strong history-aware pairwise baselines on different datasets [1]. This motivates testing a simple history component before adding encoder complexity. (2) FCESR studies influential subsequences [2]. Refining Fidelity Metrics cautions that intervention length affects comparisons [3], motivating equal-count removal controls. (3) Sampling research documents limitations of sampled rankings [4]. The pinned validation protocol must therefore remain the selection criterion, with full-catalog recommendations analyzed separately.\n\n## Directions and framework\n\nThree directions connect these insights: separate timescales, test history dependence, and preserve evidence boundaries.\n\n| Component | Existing approach | Proposed extension | Evidence boundary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Representation | SASRec sequence features | Recent-history residual | Must improve validation |\n| Diagnosis | Sampled margins | Matched history interventions | Sensitivity alone is insufficient |\n| Practical utility | Qualitative feedback | Supported/contradicted/unknown claims | Missing ownership stays unknown |\n\n## Candidate ideas\n\nScores are originality/potential/difficulty; higher difficulty means harder implementation.\n\n| Idea | Scores | Positive assessment | Negative assessment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Recent-history residual [1] | 4/7/3 | Simple combination; reusable; small model change | Established components; transfer uncertain; tuning needed |\n| Matched intervention probe [2,3] | 5/7/4 | Stronger controls; reusable diagnosis; no retraining required | Methodological extension; indirect accuracy benefit; position controls matter |\n| Evidence-aware compatibility audit | 5/6/6 | Explicit uncertainty; useful feedback schema; text-only implementation possible | Rules are proposed; sparse specifications limit coverage; extraction is difficult |\n\n## Selected idea: recent-history residual\n\nAt 0% progress, prioritize the smallest trainable change. Add a gated, recency-weighted mean of input item embeddings to each SASRec position feature. This exposes a direct recent-interest pathway while retaining the encoder’s longer-history representation. It does not infer compatibility or purchase necessity.\n\n```text\nfor each valid position t:\n    recent = last w nonpadding input items through t\n    r = sum(exp(-age / tau) * embedding(recent)) / sum(weights)\n    h[t] = sasrec_feature[t] + sigmoid(gate) * r\nscore candidates using h and the baseline item-scoring function\ntrain using the unchanged baseline loss\n```\n\nInitialize the gate near zero; choose a small window and a fixed decay before training. Compare against baseline using pinned macro validation HR@10; report category scores without claiming gains in advance. Use training-only chronological pseudo-holdouts for equal-count recent, older, and random removal, rebuilding positions consistently.\n\nRetain all four dataset routes, seeds, `os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']`, trial-local artifacts, and single-GPU execution. Update the predictor writer and compatibility view together. Preserve `DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)`, return metrics and definitions, restore evaluation state, and leave unavailable metadata breakdowns empty.",
  "idea": {
    "description": "Add a gated recency-weighted history residual to SASRec features at every valid sequence position, retaining the baseline scoring function and dataset routing.",
    "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests recent, specific preferences are sometimes underweighted. A small residual provides a directly testable recent-history pathway without requiring unavailable ownership, ratings, reviews, or compatibility labels.",
    "implementation_notes": "Keep the baseline loss, optimizer, preprocessing, seeds, and split protocol initially. Compute the residual causally from input tokens through each position; exclude padding and never include the prediction target. Use the existing item embeddings. Initialize a scalar sigmoid gate near zero and serialize the window, decay, and gate parameters. Ensure training and the generated working/predict.py instantiate identical architectures. Expose the augmented features through view.log2feats and the actual module through view.model. Preserve DiagnosisProbe's required interface and metrics/metric_definitions return structure; mark empty measurements unavailable and restore the model's prior training state. Select solely by pinned four-category macro validation HR@10. Treat training-history interventions and twenty-user feedback as exploratory diagnostics. No implementation or performance result is claimed.",
    "pseudocode": "E = item_embedding(sequence)\nF = sasrec.log2feats(sequence)\nfor t in sequence_positions:\n    valid = nonpadding positions in [max(0, t-w+1), t]\n    weights = exp(-(t-valid)/tau)\n    R[:, t] = masked_weighted_mean(E[:, valid], weights)\nH = F + sigmoid(gate) * R\nH = H * nonpadding_mask\nlogits = baseline_predict_score(H, candidates)\nloss = baseline_training_loss(logits, targets)\n# Serialize residual configuration and parameters.\n# Generate predictor with the same feature computation.\n# Compare with baseline using the host's pinned validation protocol.",
    "originality": {
      "score": 4,
      "positive": "Combines an explicit recent-history pathway with the existing diagnostic compatibility contract in a minimal experiment.",
      "negative": "Gated residuals and recency-weighted pooling are established techniques; task-specific benefit remains untested."
    },
    "future_potential": {
      "score": 7,
      "positive": "Provides a low-cost starting point for testing when direct recent evidence complements sequence encoding.",
      "negative": "A gain could reflect optimization or smoothing rather than improved intent modeling; intervention results cannot establish causality by themselves."
    },
    "code_difficulty": {
      "score": 3,
      "positive": "Requires a causal pooling operation, one gate, and matching serialization and predictor changes.",
      "negative": "Padding, positional consistency, diagnostic compatibility, and training/inference parity require careful implementation."
    }
  },
